FlashPairformer levers for Protenix 2.0.0 (opt/forward/flashpairformer) — attribution notice

This unit changes the run-time behaviour of Protenix v2.0.0 (Copyright 2024 ByteDance and/or its affiliates, Apache License 2.0,
https://github.com/bytedance/Protenix) by wrapping and replacing bound methods of the loaded model. Protenix-derived files:
- src/detref/scatter_utils.py: a modified copy of Protenix's protenix/utils/scatter_utils.py (deterministic segment-reduce variant);
  src/detref/det_segment_reduce.py beside it is written for this kit.
- levers_addon/PTXV2_LEVERS_ADDON_v1/ptx_addon_levers.py: the template distinct-evaluation lever derives from
  protenix/model/modules/pairformer.py at the commit in UPSTREAM_COMMIT.txt.
- third_party/fastln_prebuilt*/: Protenix's own fast-LayerNorm CUDA extension (protenix/model/layer_norm/kernel/*) rebuilt so that its
  kernels launch on the current CUDA stream instead of the legacy default stream; the patched sources ship beside each binary
  (patched_src/: the launch-stream argument only, arithmetic untouched). Each directory's manifest.json records the torch build it serves
  and the binary's sha256; the loader (third_party/fastln_prebuilt.py) re-checks both, and the bitwise / side-stream / graph-replay
  properties, in every process before it patches the extension in, and refuses by name otherwise (the source-built extension then serves).

Written for this kit, no third-party source included: src/ (except src/detref/), env.sh, CELLS.json, levers_addon/, and under
third_party/ the packages blockfuse_addon, fpf_smalln, fpf_pad8exact, fpf_cueq_pad8exact, protenix_fpf_msa, protenix_fpf_ditfast and
protenix_fpf_triatt_procuda (hand-written CUDA source under csrc/ using only CUDA toolkit headers and inline PTX, shipped with its prebuilt
sm_90a binary and manifest — prebuilt/NOTICE.md). Each package's own NOTICE, where present, applies to it.

Called at run time, not included or modified: PyTorch, OpenAI Triton, NVIDIA cuEquivariance (cuequivariance-torch, cuequivariance-ops-torch).
levers_addon/PTXV2_LEVERS_ADDON_v1/cueq_cache/*.json are the kit's cuEquivariance autotune cache: tile choices generated by running the
library's own TriMul autotuner on our own cards over protenix-v2 shapes (kit-generated data; no NVIDIA SDK data, no entry of the
library's packaged tables; no NVIDIA code is redistributed).
Example inputs (public_inputs/): amino-acid sequences of PDB entry 1BRS (wwPDB, public domain data) — public_inputs/PROVENANCE.md.
